        "value": "vulnerable",
        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "Akum is the principle language used at home and among friends. [...] The interviewees were unanimous that the only language used on the farm when there is no stranger present is Akum. [...] English is used most in class, but in the lower classes (1 and 2) Akum is sometimes used. Outside the class, students speak to one another in the mother tongue, Jukun, and Pidgin English. The principal of the Government Primary School-Akum said most parents send their children to school. He was positive about the introduction of the mother tongue at the elementary levels. As an Akum-speaker, he said he would not \r\nspare any efforts in assisting in such a project. [Endangerment.Certainty: 1]",
        "scale": "elcat-v2024.1"
      },
